# ============================================================================
# NoxHere environment configuration
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to .env.local for local frontend development. Server-side secrets are
# NEVER read from this file in production. Store each secret on the private
# Worker that owns it with `wrangler secret put`; see DEPLOY.md.
# ============================================================================

# === Frontend (Vite, build-time, PUBLIC — safe to ship in the bundle) ===

# GitHub App OAuth Client ID. Without it, the app falls back to PAT login.
VITE_GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=

# OAuth proxy URL — only for static frontend-only deployments that cannot run
# the /auth/github/callback route. For the NoxHere Gateway, leave blank.
VITE_OAUTH_PROXY_URL=

# Dev-server API proxy target. Where `npm run dev` forwards /api/* calls.
# Point this at your own deployed Gateway, or run the local stack.
VITE_API_TARGET=https://app.noxhere.com

# === Dev mode only (localhost) — skip OAuth and auto-login with a PAT ===
# VITE_DEV_TOKEN=ghp_your_personal_access_token
# VITE_DEV_ORG=Your-Org-Name

# ============================================================================
# === Server-side secrets — set on their owning private Worker, NOT here ===
# ============================================================================
# Listed for reference. Provider credentials belong only to Connections:
#
#   GITHUB_APP_ID              GitHub App ID (numeric), for signing App JWTs
#   GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID       GitHub App OAuth client id (server copy)
#   GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET   GitHub App OAuth client secret
#   GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY     GitHub App private key (PEM)
#   GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET      HMAC secret matching the org webhook config
#   ENCRYPTION_KEY             64-char hex key; encrypts stored refresh tokens
#                              and BYOK LLM keys at rest
#   ZHIPU_API_KEY              Default LLM provider key (orgs can override BYOK)
#   SLACK_CLIENT_ID            Shared Slack app OAuth client ID
#   SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET        Shared Slack app OAuth client secret
#   SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET       Verifies Slack Events API requests
#   POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN      Transactional email delivery token
#   POSTMARK_WEBHOOK_SECRET    Verifies Postmark delivery callbacks
#
# Shared internal assertions use NOXHERE_INTERNAL_SECRET on the Gateway,
# core API, and Connections. Optional background/AI credentials belong only
# to the capability Worker documented in DEPLOY.md.
#
# For local Worker development, put secrets in .dev.vars (gitignored).
#
# === Cloudflare bindings (configured under services/, not as env vars) ===
#   DB              D1 database
#   TASK_QUEUE      Queue producer (noxhere-tasks)
#   EVENTS_ARCHIVE  R2 bucket (noxhere-events-archive)
